// What the native Apple code needs to know about the game, in one place: the
// home screen widget asks the backend for the pilots online, the iMessage
// app links the browser game and opens the app by its scheme, and app and
// iMessage app share the round result through an app group. The values
// reach Swift through the targets' Info.plist and entitlements as
// $(APP_...) build settings, read with `AppConfig` (ios/Shared/AppConfig.swift).
//
// The first four mirror the defaults in lib/src/app/env.dart, which the Dart
// side uses; test/app/apple_config_test.dart fails when the two drift apart.
// A fork changes both (docs/forking.md). In an xcconfig `//` starts a
// comment, hence the empty $() inside each address.

APP_SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/wowtrfleffnfaiadhujj.supabase.co
APP_SUPABASE_KEY = sb_publishable__f2Lb3vqafUovQCsYilkiQ_nVNkoNhS
APP_WEB_URL = https:/$()/panzergefecht.de/play/
APP_MAX_PILOTS = 4

APP_URL_SCHEME = panzergefecht
APP_GROUP = group.de.regetskcob.wargame

// Room links on this domain open the app (universal links); the domain
// serves /.well-known/apple-app-site-association from
// store/ios/apple-app-site-association. The entitlements also list the old
// address www.regetskcob.de, whose /wargame/ links are still in the wild;
// a fork deletes that line.
APP_LINK_DOMAIN = panzergefecht.de
